{
  "schema": "bd-mutate-spec/1",
  "_comment": "Row 721. Each mutant removes one decision the age-gate cut adds. E1/E2/E3 mutants added after two independent lenses REFUTED the first round: the ENTER vocabulary was unpinned in the WIDENING direction, the gate_landing_unknown arm was unpinned, and the block report had no consumer. All anchors are zero-width on the decision and every inserted fragment is a complete statement so it parses rather than reporting INVALID. E1 is zero-width IMMEDIATELY AFTER the real ENTER_AFFORDANCE definition, so the widened redefinition shadows it: its first form anchored before the following comment and resolved COMMENT_ONLY under tests/test_row532_a_mutant_anchor_must_resolve_into_code.py, which is a mutant that edits prose and cannot be caught for the right reason.",
  "subject": "bulk_downloader/interstitial.py dismiss_gates: content-recognised age gate admits ENTER, EXIT stays refused, unreadable content is UNKNOWN, a block behind the gate is not a clearance",
  "band": [
